IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc14-part122-forfeiture`

-- ccc14-tests-part122-forfeiture.l4 -- tests for ccc14-part122-forfeiture.l4 (Criminal Code, ss 462.37 to 462.46).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run; none is copied from the module's output.
-- The conjunction cases (every condition TRUE gives the answer; each condition FALSE in turn gives the other answer) are typed by work/gen_tests_forfeiture.py from a table of expectations.
-- Y = JUST TRUE; N = JUST FALSE; NA = NOTHING (not covered).

`ccc14 Y` MEANS JUST TRUE
`ccc14 N` MEANS JUST FALSE

GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Provision of the Code`
`ccc14 test at` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF s, ""

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Imprisonment
`ccc14 test months` MEANS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, m, 0, FALSE)

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Imprisonment
`ccc14 test years` MEANS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF y, 0, 0, FALSE)

§ `s 462.37 -- Order of forfeiture of property`
-- (1) args: the offender is convicted or discharged under s 730 of a designated offence (s 462.3(1)); on application of the Attorney General; satisfied on a balance of probabilities
#ASSERT `s 462.37(1) the court must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 Y` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(1) the court must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 N` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(1) the court must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 462.37(1) the court must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 Y` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(1) the court must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 Y` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(1) the court must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` NOTHING FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) in relation to the property` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) in relation to the property` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) in relation to the property` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2) the court may make an order of forfeiture under subsection (1) in relation to the property` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2.01) args: convicted of an offence described in (2.02); application of the Attorney General; the property is identified in the application; (a) pattern of criminal activity; (b) income cannot reasonably account for the property
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01) the court must order that the property of the offender identified by the Attorney General be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 Y` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01) the court must order that the property of the offender identified by the Attorney General be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 Y` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01) the court must order that the property of the offender identified by the Attorney General be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 Y` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01) the court must order that the property of the offender identified by the Attorney General be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 Y` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01) the court must order that the property of the offender identified by the Attorney General be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 Y` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01) the court must order that the property of the offender identified by the Attorney General be forfeited to Her Majesty` `ccc14 N` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01) the court must order that the property of the offender identified by the Attorney General be forfeited to Her Majesty` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2.01)(a) args: the date the proceedings were commenced; the date of the pattern of criminal activity
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01)(a) the pattern of criminal activity is within 10 years before the proceedings were commenced` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 462.37(2.01)(a) the pattern of criminal activity is within 10 years before the proceedings were commenced` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2016) EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
