§ `The regulative rule, run with #TRACE`
-- 462.42(1): the person MAY apply WITHIN 30 (days from the forfeiture). Applying on day 30 is in time; on day 31 the permission has lapsed (a MAY that lapses unused is FULFILLED, without consequence, on the stable binary).
#TRACE `s 462.42(1) the right to apply within thirty days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 462.42 a person who claims an interest in property that is forfeited to Her Majesty` DOES `s 462.42(1) apply by notice in writing to a judge for an order under subsection (4)` AT 30
#TRACE `s 462.42(1) the right to apply within thirty days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 462.42 a person who claims an interest in property that is forfeited to Her Majesty` DOES `s 462.42(1) apply by notice in writing to a judge for an order under subsection (4)` AT 31
#TRACE `s 462.42(1) the right to apply within thirty days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
